<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ reports NZ$134.3 mln trade deficit in January.</title>
<headline>NZ reports NZ$134.3 mln trade deficit in January.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Thursday released the following provisional statistics for New Zealand external merchandise trade for January:</p>
<p>(Figures are rounded)</p>
<p>Monthly series:</p>
<p>		Jan 1997	    Dec 1996	     Jan 1996</p>
<p>Balance    -$134.3 mln	  $30.0 mln	   -$245.0 mln</p>
<p>Exports     $1.46 bln	   $1.72 bln	    $1.40 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.59 bln	   $1.69 bln	    $1.65 bln</p>
<p>		Yr-to-Jan 1997    Yr-to-Dec 1996     Yr-to-Jan 1996</p>
<p>Balance    -$239.1 million    -$349.8 million    -$602.4 million</p>
<p>Exports     $21.10 bln	  $21.05 bln	   $20.88 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $21.34 bln	  $21.40 bln	   $21.48 bln</p>
<p>Trend series:</p>
<p>		Jan 1997	    Dec 1996	     Jan 1996</p>
<p>Balance    +$17.0 million     +$28.3 million     -$104.4 million</p>
<p>Exports     $1.75 billion     $1.76 bln	    $1.69 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.73 billion     $1.73 bln	    $1.79 bln</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4) 473 4746</p>
</text>
